Spec: Actual Windows public SDK connection verification

Purpose:
  Verify formal RPC and SDK business delivery over owned authenticated FRP routes.

Owns:
  ./FormalWindowsFixture.cs

Must:
  In dynamic mode observe same-scope runtime reuse and owned cleanup after network invalidation and grant loss without static visitor configuration.
  Query an original successful open through the typed SDK on a declaration-only control host without formal capability, using the same actual OS caller.
  Run only in the explicit Windows fixture, retaining the existing isolated Android fixture scope and backend counts.
  Require independently approved exact local visitor grants and current publisher/server authority before any formal business.
  Verify three 64 MiB transfers, exact path counters, retained open/attach operations, single-use pipes, independent cancellation, injected generation change and active local access revocation.
  Record simulated generation changes separately from physical network observation and keep this same-process SDK fixture distinct from independent Windows application acceptance.
